# Title: summary, imperative, start upper case, no final period, up to 50 chars, blank line afterwards.
#
# Commit types (feat not used):
#
#  - new: when a new log or assigment appears, probably involves a change in readme to pin important parts.
#
#  - chore: small task without new information, like syntatic fixes or pinning.
#
#  - format: writting format change.
#
# Commit scopes: readme, asssiment and log.
#
# Body: description and reasoning, without much details. No wrap. Co-authorings at end.
#
# Co-authored-by: name <foo@bar.com>
#
# References:
#
#  - Conventional Commits Specification: https://www.conventionalcommits.org
#